From: zigzag go-port/rustcore
Subject: [PATCH 4] fix(send_queue): keep a room's sends in order when one fails (backport of #6843)

Upstream matrix-org/matrix-rust-sdk#6843, "send queue: preserve ordering when a
request fails to send" (merged 2026-08-27 as a61d2383e, released in matrix-sdk
0.19.0), applied to our base 96ffd1a0b as it is. Only the line offsets differ,
plus one hunk whose context lacks a field (FinishUpload's extra_content) that
upstream added after our base.

- A request that failed for good (wedged) now blocks the requests queued after
  it in the same room until it is unwedged or aborted. Before, it was skipped,
  so later messages went out ahead of it.
- A failed media upload's error now shows on the media event's local echo.
- HTTP 520 is transient again: retried, and kept in the queue instead of wedged.
- Failing to load the next request from the store backs off 250 ms instead of
  retrying in a tight loop.

Upstream's changelog note (changelog.d/6843.changed.md) is left out. Drop this
patch when the base moves to matrix-sdk >= 0.19.0, which contains it.
